## Description

thc1006

opened on Jul 12, 2026

Issue body actions

Describe the bug

`i2s_buf_write()` documents two error returns that it has made unreachable, and blocks forever instead.

The doxygen in `include/zephyr/drivers/i2s.h`:

    ` * @retval -EIO The interface is not in READY or RUNNING state.
     * @retval -EBUSY Returned without waiting.
     * @retval -EAGAIN Waiting period timed out.
Call `i2s_buf_write()` N+1 times without starting the stream. The N+1st call never returns.

Expected behaviour

Either honour the documented contract -- allocate with the caller's `i2s_config.timeout` and return `-EAGAIN`/`-ENOMEM` when it expires -- or, if blocking forever is genuinely the intended semantic, say so in the doxygen and delete the unreachable `-ENOMEM` branch. Right now the header and the code disagree, and the header is the one applications are written against.

I have not sent a patch because the choice between those two is an API decision, not a bug fix, and it is not mine to make. Happy to do the work either way once someone who owns `i2s_common.c` says which.

Environment

Found on ESP32-S3 (Zephyr 4.4.0), but the code is generic and the same on `main` (`0a9cc79`).

