## Description

tmon-nordic

opened on Oct 10, 2023

Issue body actions

Describe the bug
Data written with i2s_nrfx_write() can appear out-of-order (i.e. data passed in later call to i2s_nrfx_write() can be sent before earlier call to i2s_nrfx_write()) on the i2s bus.

To Reproduce
Create application that uses I2S in TX only mode with 3 i2s slab buffers. Keep feeding the buffer at varying time. The issue was observed in USB->I2S application where the USB clock was running slightly faster than ACLK (i.e. 1 ms according to USB took slightly shorter "real world time" than 1 ms according to ACLK) which allowed to hit the issue once every 160 seconds (160000 frames).

Expected behavior
Data on i2s bus appear in the same order as written to i2s_nrfx_write().

Impact
Clearly audible audio glitches with 48 kHz audio where single i2s buffer holds 48 samples for each channel.

